alue of an integer coordinate determinant, so the area is an integer or half-integer. For example, (0,0), (1,0), (0,1) give area 1/2, so it need not be an integer.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p149"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1958_AMC_12_Q35","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_082","cnm_p148"],"id":"compare-trapezoid-areas","label":"Compare areas above a horizontal baseline","methodDirectNodeIds":{"compare-trapezoid-areas":["cnm_084","cnm_003","cnm_p149","cnm_p150"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_084","cnm_003","cnm_p149","cnm_p150","cnm_082","cnm_p148"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:99e0976bdb69967a73513953"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 40¢ per cookie","reason":"Art's cookie area is (3+5)×3/2=12 square inches; Roger's is 4×2=8 square inches. The batch therefore has total area 12×12=144 square inches, giving Roger 144/8=18 cookies. To match Art's revenue of 12×60=720 cents, each must cost 720/18=40 cents.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p149"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2003_AMC_8_Q09","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p110","cnm_p106"],"id":"m1","label":"Find the batch size and revenue","methodDirectNodeIds":{"m1":["cnm_p149","cnm_p089","cnm_p214","cnm_p111"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p149","cnm_p089","cnm_p214","cnm_p111","cnm_p110","cnm_p106"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:99e0976bdb69967a73513953"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C: 5","reason":"Write AB=a, DC=d, and EF=(a+d)/2. Equal heights give (a+EF)/(EF+d)=2, so a=EF+2d and therefore a=5d.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_p149"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2005_AMC_10B_Q23","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_034","cnm_040"],